WEBVTT

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.240
Hey, Aura, remember we've discussed this idea

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.810
of a coffee subscription service called Slow
Lane before?

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.680
Yeah, I remember the name. Coffee
subscription, right?

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.880
Yeah, exactly. I'm ready to get started,

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.010
but where do we even start with something like
that?

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.720
All right, so I've pulled up your earlier Slow
Lane work,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.620
and I think the easiest place to start is with
the look and feel.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.560
Actually, let's make sure the voice and tone
matches the name

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.760
so it feels like a slow lane. You know what I
mean?

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.420
Yeah, totally. I read that as unhurried,

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.280
grounded, maybe a touch playful.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.290
Wait, what do you actually think about the
idea?

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.380
Do you think it has potential, or am I wasting
time here?

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.350
I think it has real potential. People like
coffee,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.860
and they like a calm, intentional brand vibe.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.660
And Slow Lane already tells a story.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.500
We can shape it into something that feels
distinct.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.140
What's nudging you to wonder if it's a waste?

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.140
I just never started, and I'm not very
confident about this idea.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.140
Yeah, that makes sense.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.320
If you want, we can start with a quick,
low-pressure step,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.460
like a simple visual direction or a
one-sentence brand promise.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.580
Let's start with a simple visual direction.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.440
I like to see things visually before we
proceed.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.490
The board's ready with the colors, serif name,
tagline,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.820
and a few mood shots, plus a little playful
snail.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.660
I actually quite like it.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.450
I'd love to explore this direction further

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.000
with a few more visuals and a simple promo
video.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.060
I'd love to launch this on Instagram.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.620
Can you prepare the materials for a launch
kit?

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.140
Okay, the visual is ready. You'll see it in
your folder.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.470
An unboxing flat lay, a slow morning shot,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.060
a launch graphic, and a short doorstep clip.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:51.650
I'd start with a single strong visual, maybe
the ready launch post,

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.570
then follow with the clip as a second beat,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.580
building a gentle rhythm that fits the brand.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.460
I love this. Something slow is brewing. Such a
cool teaser.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.510
Quick status update. Your three feed posts,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.340
two stories, and the vertical reel are ready.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.820
I've also saved captions and hashtags.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.040
I think I'm good for now. Thank you so much.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.360
You're welcome. Good luck with the launch.
